# Deployment Guide

## Prerequisites

- AWS CLI installed and configured (`aws configure`)
- An existing EC2 Key Pair in us-east-1
- Bash shell (Linux/Mac/WSL)

---

## Step-by-Step

### 1. Clone this repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/intent-classifier-aws-deploy
cd intent-classifier-aws-deploy
```

### 2. Edit configuration
Open `infrastructure/setup.sh` and update:
```bash
AWS_REGION="us-east-1"
KEY_NAME="your-key-pair-name"
```

### 3. Run the setup
```bash
bash infrastructure/setup.sh
```

### 4. Wait for initialization
The EC2 instance takes 5-10 minutes to:
- Install dependencies
- Clone the repository
- Train the model
- Start Gunicorn and Nginx

### 5. Verify health
```bash
aws elbv2 describe-target-health \
  --target-group-arn <TG_ARN> \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --query "TargetHealthDescriptions[0].TargetHealth"
```
Expected: `"State": "healthy"`

### 6. Test the API
```bash
curl -X POST http://<ALB-DNS> \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"text": "book a flight to New York"}'
```

---

## Teardown

To avoid AWS charges, delete all resources:

```bash
# Delete ASG
aws autoscaling delete-auto-scaling-group --auto-scaling-group-name mlops-autoscaling --force-delete --region us-east-1

# Delete ALB
aws elbv2 delete-load-balancer --load-balancer-arn <ALB_ARN> --region us-east-1

# Delete Target Group
aws elbv2 delete-target-group --target-group-arn <TG_ARN> --region us-east-1

# Delete Launch Template
aws ec2 delete-launch-template --launch-template-name intent-classifier-lt --region us-east-1

# Delete Security Group, Subnets, IGW, VPC
aws ec2 delete-security-group --group-id <SG_ID> --region us-east-1
aws ec2 delete-subnet --subnet-id <SUBNET_ID1> --region us-east-1
aws ec2 delete-subnet --subnet-id <SUBNET_ID2> --region us-east-1
aws ec2 detach-internet-gateway --internet-gateway-id <IGW_ID> --vpc-id <VPC_ID> --region us-east-1
aws ec2 delete-internet-gateway --internet-gateway-id <IGW_ID> --region us-east-1
aws ec2 delete-vpc --vpc-id <VPC_ID> --region us-east-1
```
